    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes (1 run, 0 failures), with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation.\n\n**The rule:** When a newly created owner is *not* a hard duplicate (its identity key doesn't collide) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone, the owner is still created, with `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (lowest id if several match). Otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false` and `possibleDuplicateOf` is absent. A postcode is required on both sides, so an owner without one is never flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) persistent fields with getters/setters.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 added `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)`, invoked in `addOwner` right after the hard-duplicate identity check and before the other derived fields are assigned.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them (MapStruct maps them automatically by name).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate`) reads the flags back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and passes.",
